[assembly: AssemblyMetadata("LongDescription", "**Author: Massimo Mainini**\n\nDigital StarGate Observatory Telemetry Exporter is the read-only telemetry integration plugin for the Digital StarGate observatory in N.I.N.A. It consolidates observatory status into a single local projection used by the Digital StarGate monitoring architecture.\n\nThe plugin observes and exports: dome connection and shutter state; mount connection, park/home/tracking state and pier side; imaging camera connection, exposure state, sensor temperature, cooler state and cooler power; weather data including temperature, humidity, dew point, wind speed and gusts, atmospheric pressure, cloud cover, rain rate and sky temperature; the N.I.N.A. SafetyMonitor state as an observation only; TS Shelter/J6 power evidence including mains presence and power-fault state; network health including active link, gateway and Internet reachability, latency, DNS resolution, VPN and LTE failover evidence; and instrumental sky brightness/SQM in magnitudes per square arcsecond from the approved AAG CloudWatcher SOLO lightmpsas source, including source timestamp, freshness, quality, serial number and firmware identity.\n\nAll telemetry is normalized with explicit CURRENT, STALE or UNKNOWN quality semantics and is exported through the unified nina-observatory-status.json projection for downstream Observatory Status processing. Invalid, unavailable or stale measurements fail to UNKNOWN/null rather than being estimated from proxy values.\n\nThe plugin is strictly read-only: it does not command the dome, mount, camera, power system, router or CloudWatcher, does not modify equipment configuration and does not replace the local physical Safety Authority or observatory interlocks. SQM and other monitoring data are observability/scientific signals only and never authorize roof or equipment operations.")]
